    <h2>Why image compression matters</h2>
    <p>Image Compressor is a free, privacy-first tool that shrinks JPG, PNG, and WebP images directly in your browser — nothing is uploaded, nothing is stored, and no account or software installation is required. You can be compressing images within seconds of opening the page.</p>
    <p><strong>Why image size matters.</strong> Images make up a large share of the weight of most web pages. Oversized images slow down load times, consume mobile data, hurt your Core Web Vitals, and push your site down in search rankings. Compressing an image before you upload it is one of the fastest, cheapest ways to make a website faster — and it costs you nothing.</p>
    <p><strong>Who it is for.</strong> Web developers and site owners who want faster pages and better SEO; designers and content creators who need optimized assets; bloggers, sellers, and marketers who upload product or hero images to platforms with strict size limits; and anyone who simply wants a smaller file to share over email or chat.</p>
    <p><strong>How it works.</strong> Choose a compression level — Normal, Strong, or Extreme — depending on how small you need the file and how much quality you can trade away. Pick an output format (WebP is recommended for the smallest files). Then drag in one image for a live before-and-after preview, or drop in several at once to batch-compress and download everything as a single ZIP archive. Everything runs locally, so your images never leave your device.</p>
